From ec762957e7141ea460b9365ce636e80d51fcdec5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 11:57:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] transports/handlers: route inference through BifrostRouter
 (per-request runtime acquire)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace direct h.client.X calls with h.router.Acquire(ctx) + defer release
across the HTTP inference handlers so multi-tenant deployments can dispatch
each request to the per-tenant Bifrost runtime resolved by upstream
middleware. Single-tenant deployments are unaffected: NewSingleTenantRouter
returns the shared client with a no-op release.

inference.go
- Add clientOrFail helper that acquires the runtime and writes a 500 on
  failure. All non-streaming entry points (text/chat/responses/embeddings/
  rerank/ocr/speech/transcription/countTokens/image*/file*/batch*/
  container*/video*) now acquire upfront, defer release, and call methods
  on the returned client instead of h.client.
- handleStreamingResponse gains a releaseBifrost callback; the seven
  streaming entry points (Text/Chat/Responses/Speech/Transcription/
  ImageGen/ImageEdit Stream) acquire before invoking the stream getter
  and pass release through so the runtime stays pinned for the SSE
  goroutine's lifetime.

asyncinference.go
- Move runtime acquisition inside each SubmitJob closure so the executor
  resolves the tenant at execution time, not at submit time. Wrap
  Acquire failures in a BifrostError via the new asyncAcquireError helper.

mcpinference.go
- Port the clientOrFail pattern to MCPInferenceHandler and switch
  executeChatMCPTool / executeResponsesMCPTool to the acquired client.

Out of scope (intentional): admin handlers (providers.go, mcp.go),
realtime/websocket handlers (wsrealtime.go, wsresponses.go,
webrtc_realtime.go, realtime_client_secrets.go) — those continue to use
the back-pointer h.client; they are not part of the HTTP REST inference
plane this patch covers.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
